## Fix Inference materialise-to-graph for Delta triple store

Context: Inference → "Materialise to graph" failed on ``triple_store_backend=databricks``
because ``ReasoningService`` inserted into the logical graph name (``Domain_V5``) while
the Delta backend only materialized ``…_data`` at build time — the ``…_inferred``
companion TABLE and union read VIEW were never created.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaFlatStore.py
   Route ``insert_triples`` to ``…_inferred``; ensure companion TABLE + ``…_graph`` VIEW.
2. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/materialize.py
   ``ensure_inferred_table`` and ``ensure_graph_view`` DDL helpers.
3. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/_table_naming.py
   ``graph_view_fqn`` (``…_graph`` = ``_data`` ∪ ``_inferred``).
4. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaTripleStoreBuildPipeline.py
   Create inferred TABLE and graph VIEW on build (truncate inferred on full rebuild).
5. src/back/core/helpers/SQLHelpers.py
   ``effective_graph_query_table`` returns ``…_graph`` when ``include_inferred``.
6. src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py
   Pass domain/settings into ``DeltaFlatStore``.
7. src/front/templates/settings.html
   Document ``…_graph`` union VIEW in Delta object list.
8. tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_flat_store.py
   Inferred routing and synced-table resolution tests.
9. tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_package.py, test_triple_store_backend_config.py
   DDL and resolver coverage.

